        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12503356/comment/13035361",
          "id": "13035361",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=uschindler",
            "name": "uschindler",
            "key": "thetaphi",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956"
            },
            "displayName": "Uwe Schindler",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "It's fine, commit it!\n\nWe may look for usage of the version field in SegmentInfos, and use this comparator there (especially e.g. my new one for upgrades or the standard IndexTooOldException stuff).\n\nBut I think that should be a new issue.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=uschindler",
            "name": "uschindler",
            "key": "thetaphi",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956"
            },
            "displayName": "Uwe Schindler",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2011-05-18T13:18:22.188+0000",
          "updated": "2011-05-18T13:18:22.188+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12503356/comment/13035370",
          "id": "13035370",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "body": "Hey guys, does this affect LUCENE-2921 (or vice versa)?\n\nBasically, I thought that we should stop writing version header in files and just use the release version as a header.\n\nRobert, I don't think we are allowed to change index format versions on bug-fix releases and even if we do, that same bug fix would go into the 3.x release so it would still know how to read 3.1.1? Perhaps that was your point and I missed it ...",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "created": "2011-05-18T13:27:25.376+0000",
          "updated": "2011-05-18T13:27:25.376+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12503356/comment/13035376",
          "id": "13035376",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=uschindler",
            "name": "uschindler",
            "key": "thetaphi",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956"
            },
            "displayName": "Uwe Schindler",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "Shai: we should not change index format, but it still feels bad not to have a correct version comparison API. With this patch you can even compare 3.0 against only 3 or 3.0.0.0.0 and they will be equal. And once we are at version 10, a simple string compare is a bad idea :-)\n\nThats why Robert and me are against pure string comparisons.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=uschindler",
            "name": "uschindler",
            "key": "thetaphi",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956"
            },
            "displayName": "Uwe Schindler",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2011-05-18T13:30:37.146+0000",
          "updated": "2011-05-18T13:30:37.146+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12503356/comment/13035378",
          "id": "13035378",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "{quote}\nHey guys, does this affect LUCENE-2921 (or vice versa)?\n{quote}\n\nHi Shai, I think this helps LUCENE-2921. This is a comparator to use, when you want to examine the release version that created the segment (the one you added in LUCENE-2720). Its guaranteed to compare correctly if say, we we released 3.10, and also if the number of trailing zeros etc are different.\n\nIn other words, if you implement LUCENE-2921 I think the idea is typically you will want to use this comparator when examining the version string.\n\n{quote}\nRobert, I don't think we are allowed to change index format versions on bug-fix releases and even if we do, that same bug fix would go into the 3.x release so it would still know how to read 3.1.1? Perhaps that was your point and I missed it ...\n{quote}\n\nOn LUCENE-3012, I've proposed a fix-for version for Lucene 3.2. But we can discuss on that issue.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2011-05-18T13:35:07.167+0000",
          "updated": "2011-05-18T13:35:07.167+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12503356/comment/13035379",
          "id": "13035379",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "body": "Yes, that makes sense. I can use that API in LUCENE-2921. Thanks a lot for saving me some effort :).",
